/T (In collaboration with the Yashraj Foundation \(YRF\), we launched a program in the village of Anvir to connect volunteers with students via voice calls. However, frequent network issues led us to reconsider this approach. Inspired by the Adgaon model, we adopted a similar strategy in Anvir, but instead of using laptops or tablets, we provided basic hand sets, which were generously donated. The Read-a-story  program is held on Saturdays after school & on Sundays, with two sessions each day. The YRF program enrolled 60 students, who were paired with around 40-45 volunteers.)
/E (In collaboration with the Yashraj Foundation \(YRF\), we launched a program in the village of Anvir to connect volunteers with students via voice calls. However, frequent network issues led us to reconsider this approach. Inspired by the Adgaon model, we adopted a similar strategy in Anvir, but instead of using laptops or tablets, we provided basic hand sets, which were generously donated. The Read-a-story  program is held on Saturdays after school & on Sundays, with two sessions each day. The YRF program enrolled 60 students, who were paired with around 40-45 volunteers.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
