312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Tribal Girls Government Hostels in Agar & Talasari, located in Palghar, serve as vital residential facilities for tribal girls pursuing higher education at various colleges in the Talasari region. These girls are often first-generation learners, & for many, the first in their families to attend college. Managed by the government through the Integrated Tribal Development Project, the hostels provide free boarding & lodging, ensuring these young women have a secure place to live while they focus on their studies. Each hostel has a capacity of approximately 200 girls, who are enrolled in 11th & 12th grades, as well as 1st, 2nd, & 3rd-year college programs across arts, commerce, & science streams. Despite the hostels being located 2 kilometers from the main town, the girls regularly walk to their colleges & other places within a 3-4 kilometer radius. Recognizing the critical importance of English proficiency for future career opportunities, Read-a-story introduced an English reading program at both hostels. This initiative aims to help the girls strengthen their English language skills, which are essential for their academic success & broader career prospects. With a focus on empowering these young women, the program has been well-received, & Read-a-story plans to expand it to other hostels in the near future, further supporting the educational aspirations of tribal girls in the region.)
/E (The Tribal Girls Government Hostels in Agar & Talasari, located in Palghar, serve as vital residential facilities for tribal girls pursuing higher education at various colleges in the Talasari region. These girls are often first-generation learners, & for many, the first in their families to attend college. Managed by the government through the Integrated Tribal Development Project, the hostels provide free boarding & lodging, ensuring these young women have a secure place to live while they focus on their studies. Each hostel has a capacity of approximately 200 girls, who are enrolled in 11th & 12th grades, as well as 1st, 2nd, & 3rd-year college programs across arts, commerce, & science streams. Despite the hostels being located 2 kilometers from the main town, the girls regularly walk to their colleges & other places within a 3-4 kilometer radius. Recognizing the critical importance of English proficiency for future career opportunities, Read-a-story introduced an English reading program at both hostels. This initiative aims to help the girls strengthen their English language skills, which are essential for their academic success & broader career prospects. With a focus on empowering these young women, the program has been well-received, & Read-a-story plans to expand it to other hostels in the near future, further supporting the educational aspirations of tribal girls in the region.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
