/T (Savitribai Phule Mahila Ekatma Mandal \(SPMESM\) and Read-a-story \(RAS\) share a common mission to enhance English reading proficiency among first-generation learners from rural backgrounds. These students, who come from marginalized communities, often face educational challenges due to their socio-economic conditions. Most of the children's parents are employed as farmers or laborers, making it difficult for families to provide academic support at home.)
/E (Savitribai Phule Mahila Ekatma Mandal \(SPMESM\) and Read-a-story \(RAS\) share a common mission to enhance English reading proficiency among first-generation learners from rural backgrounds. These students, who come from marginalized communities, often face educational challenges due to their socio-economic conditions. Most of the children's parents are employed as farmers or laborers, making it difficult for families to provide academic support at home.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The joint program between SPMESM and RAS currently enrolls 350 students, offering personalized English tutoring to help bridge the learning gap. A significant portion of the students are from farm laborer families, where parents earn modest wages through daily work in nearby fields. Others come from small farmer households, where their parents manage family-owned farms. Given these backgrounds, access to quality education, particularly in English, is limited.)
/E (The joint program between SPMESM and RAS currently enrolls 350 students, offering personalized English tutoring to help bridge the learning gap. A significant portion of the students are from farm laborer families, where parents earn modest wages through daily work in nearby fields. Others come from small farmer households, where their parents manage family-owned farms. Given these backgrounds, access to quality education, particularly in English, is limited.)
