/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (At Read-a-story, level setting is a key process to ensure that students are paired with appropriate reading materials and volunteers. This evaluation involves assessing each student's English reading ability and assigning them a corresponding level. By understanding their proficiency, we can customize our teaching approach to ensure students are sufficiently challenged to make progress without feeling overwhelmed. In response to the challenges posed by the pandemic, Read-a-story adapted its evaluation process. While in-person assessments may not always be feasible, conducting evaluations over the phone has proven to be an effective and innovative solution, allowing us to continue supporting students remotely. )
/E (At Read-a-story, level setting is a key process to ensure that students are paired with appropriate reading materials and volunteers. This evaluation involves assessing each student's English reading ability and assigning them a corresponding level. By understanding their proficiency, we can customize our teaching approach to ensure students are sufficiently challenged to make progress without feeling overwhelmed. In response to the challenges posed by the pandemic, Read-a-story adapted its evaluation process. While in-person assessments may not always be feasible, conducting evaluations over the phone has proven to be an effective and innovative solution, allowing us to continue supporting students remotely. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
