/T (I was latched to the children from Adgaon, a remote village in Maharashtra. I would get into a Zoom call with them twice weekly and conduct reading sessions. Amidst a patchy network and an acute communication gap, we read together. I have picked up a few Marathi words in the process apart from their endearing smiles towards the end of the session. It's a win-win situation.)
